'''NED-B''' was a [[Gender|masculine]] [[loader droid]] that operated on the [[planet]] [[Mapuzo]] during the [[Imperial Era]]. The [[droid]] worked with [[Tala Durith]] in an underground movement known as the [[Hidden Path]], which helped [[Smuggler|smuggle]] surviving [[Jedi]] to safety. He kept watch over a safehouse hidden within the droid maintenance building of a [[Mapuzo mining village|mining village]].<ref name="Kenobi III" />

==Biography==
[[File:NED-B.png|thumb|left|200px|NED-B on Mapuzo]]
NED-B aided the fugitives [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]] and [[Leia Skywalker Organa Solo|Leia Organa]]<ref name="Kenobi III" /> in [[9 BBY]].<ref name="Date" /> When [[stormtrooper]]s searched the safehouse, NED-B discreetly grabbed a [[Hammer (tool)|hammer]], preparing to fight if necessary. Although a stormtrooper interrogated him, the [[trooper]]s soon left. Later, he helped Durith save Kenobi from the [[Sith Lord]] [[Anakin Skywalker|Darth Vader]].<ref name="Kenobi III" />

He escaped with the [[Hidden Path]] to [[Jabiim]],<ref name="Kenobi IV">{{Kenobi|Part IV}}</ref> where he later [[Death|sacrificed]] himself in [[Attack on Jabiim|battle]] with stormtroopers to buy [[time]] for the other members of the Path to escape. His final act was to shield Durith from the oncoming stormtroopers before dying in her [[Limb|arms]].<ref name="Kenobi V" />

==Characteristics==
[[File:Databank-NEDB.png|thumb|right|300px|NED-B wields an E-5 blaster rifle in battle.]]
NED-B was not capable of vocalizing but was still a capable droid. Despite the fact that his official designation was NED-B, the [[Aurebesh]] inscription on his chest read "NED-W,"<ref name="Kenobi III" /> while "NED 1" was printed on his back.<ref name="Kenobi V">{{Kenobi|Part V}}</ref>

{{Droid-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
{{Quote|Ned-B is a loader droid. We kind of harken to our own forklift in the shop and use some of those cues in his paint job with the chipped paint.|[[John Rosengrant]]|<ref name="Designing the Galaxy">{{HomeVideoCite|set=Obi-Wan Kenobi: The Complete Series|featurette=Designing the Galaxy}}</ref>}}
[[File:Ned-BBehindTheScenes.png|thumb|left|250px|Deborah Chow, [[Ewan McGregor]], and NED-B in the Path's hideout on Mapuzo]]
NED-B was first pictured in the teaser trailer for the ''[[Star Wars: Obi-Wan Kenobi]]'' television series, which was released on [[March 9]], [[2022]].<ref name="Teaser">{{SWYouTube|TWTfhyvzTx0|Obi-Wan Kenobi &#124; Teaser Trailer &#124; Disney+|sw_url=video/teaser-trailer-obi-wan-kenobi}}</ref> He first appeared in the [[Part III|third episode]] of the series, which aired on [[June 1]], 2022.<ref name="D23">{{D23|url=everything-new-you-can-stream-on-disney-in-june-2022|text=Everything New You Can Stream on Disney+ in June 2022}}</ref>

The sounds for NED-B's movements originated from a bread maker. Director [[Deborah Chow]] told sound designer and editor [[Jon Borland]] to make the sounds feel sad when NED-B died in the series.<ref name="Saga chronicles">{{SW|url=news/saga-chronicles-obi-wan-kenobi-sound|text=Saga Chronicles: Skywalker Sound's Danielle Dupre and Jon Borland on Their ''Obi-Wan Kenobi'' Journey}}</ref>

